# Wave W17-V (Route 207): switchback sand — switchback sand with the zigzag tread drawn in the kind: a pale climbing sand whose darker tread cuts corner to corner in a zigzag, the switchback drawn into the path itself (design-authorised: a clear connected path of pale sand running end to end, climbing; the fallfloor discipline — the design lives in the kind’s art). The fleet’s only zigzag path: split from every straight sand by the tread itself, and from Route 208’s plain rest sand by effort (this path climbs, that one rests).
